# .gitleaksignore — KNOWN FALSE POSITIVES, each with its reason.
#
# ⭐ WHY AN ALLOWLIST EXISTS AT ALL: a hook that fires on a known-good finding every time
# someone touches the file trains the `--no-verify` habit, and a routinely-bypassed hook is
# WORSE than no hook — everyone believes it is running. Every entry here must carry a reason.
# If you cannot write the reason, it is not a false positive; fix the finding instead.
#
# ⚠️ FINGERPRINTS EMBED A LINE NUMBER (`file:rule:line`), so they BREAK when lines shift.
